    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "The model makes one vector per token, not per chunk. Seven tokens give seven vectors — then mean pooling averages them into one chunk vector.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B02",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.11,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B02",
        "at": "2026-09-11T16:11:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "You could embed one chunk at a time. Instead, stack sixty-four rows and push them through the same weight matrix together.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B03",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.06,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B03",
        "at": "2026-09-11T16:11:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "The result from the project: sixty-four separate multiplies took fifteen milliseconds, one batched multiply took one point two. Twelve and a half times faster.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.49,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04",
        "at": "2026-09-11T16:11:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "And the arithmetic is identical — seventy-five million operations both ways. The speedup isn't less math; the bottleneck is memory bandwidth.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B05",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.03,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B05",
        "at": "2026-09-11T16:11:05"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "LIST",
      "narration_text": "So at scale: batch first, it's the biggest win. Stream in shards for bounded memory. And content-hash chunks so you only re-embed what changed.",
